<HelpChapterSection Id="profile">
    <HelpTopicSection Id="profile-overview">
        <p>Open <span class="help-ui">Profile</span> in the menu or click your name at the bottom of the side menu. The profile has two tabs: <span class="help-ui">Profile</span> and <span class="help-ui">Security</span>.</p>
        <p>On the <span class="help-ui">Profile</span> tab:</p>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Card</strong> — full name, email, the <span class="help-ui">2FA enabled</span> badge and the time of your last sign-in.</li>
            <li><strong>Positions</strong> — all your positions: title, unit and role. Your primary position is marked <span class="help-ui">Primary</span>. Click a position to open the unit's page. If you have no positions — “No positions assigned. Contact the HR department.”</li>
            <li><strong>Available modules</strong> — the modules of the cabinet open to you. Expand <span class="help-ui">All my permissions</span> to see each permission with its description.</li>
            <li><strong>Contacts</strong> — your email (cannot be changed, it is your login) and <span class="help-ui">Phone</span>. Enter the number in the +380… format and click <span class="help-ui">Save</span> — “Phone number saved.” appears.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Your name and positions are managed by the HR department. If the data is wrong or you lack access to a module, contact them or the system administrator.</p>
        <p><strong>Interface language.</strong> The cabinet is available in Ukrainian and English. In the <span class="help-ui">Interface language</span> card, choose <span class="help-ui">Українська</span> or <span class="help-ui">English</span> and click <span class="help-ui">Apply</span>. The language is saved in your profile and applies on all your devices. Before signing in, you can change the language with the button in the top-right corner of the sign-in page.</p>
    </HelpTopicSection>

    <HelpTopicSection Id="profile-photo">
        <p>A profile photo is required: colleagues see it next to your name in documents and signing routes, news and comments, the structure, user lists and the audit log. Until you have a photo, the cabinet opens the <span class="help-ui">Add a profile photo</span> page after you sign in — the other sections become available as soon as you save one.</p>
        <ol class="help-steps">
            <li>Click <span class="help-ui">Choose or drop a photo</span> and pick a file: JPEG, PNG, WebP, AVIF or GIF up to 15 MB.</li>
            <li>In the round frame, drag the photo with the mouse or a finger (or the arrow keys) and zoom with the slider or the mouse wheel so the face is inside the circle.</li>
            <li>Click <span class="help-ui">Save photo</span> — “Profile photo saved” appears.</li>
        </ol>
        <p>To change the photo later, click the photo on the <span class="help-ui">Profile</span> tab (the camera icon). The new photo replaces the previous one everywhere, and the old one is deleted.</p>
        <p>The photo is compressed on the server to AVIF (a few kilobytes), and the image metadata, including location, is removed. Only signed-in users of the cabinet can see photos.</p>
    </HelpTopicSection>

    <HelpTopicSection Id="profile-security">
        <p>The <span class="help-ui">Security</span> tab has four cards. The first three are described below, the <span class="help-ui">Other devices</span> card — in “<a href="/help#profile-sessions">Signing out on other devices</a>”.</p>
        <h4>Password</h4>
        <p>The <span class="help-ui">Change password</span> button opens the password change form (see “<a href="/help#account-change-password">Changing your password</a>”).</p>
        <h4>Two-factor authentication</h4>
        <p>Shows the status: <span class="help-ui">Enabled</span> or <span class="help-ui">Not set up</span>. Changed your phone? Ask the administrator to reset your authenticator — you will set up the new one the next time you sign in.</p>
        <h4>Recovery codes</h4>
        <p>Shows how many codes are left. If you are running low on codes or suspect someone has seen them, generate a new set:</p>
        <ol class="help-steps">
            <li>Open the authenticator app and enter the current 6-digit code in the field next to the <span class="help-ui">New codes</span> button. This is an extra confirmation: without your phone the codes cannot be changed, even by someone who has access to your signed-in browser.</li>
            <li>Click <span class="help-ui">New codes</span> and confirm “Generate new codes? The old ones will stop working.”</li>
            <li>10 new codes appear. Click <span class="help-ui">Copy</span> and save them — they will not be shown again. The old codes no longer work.</li>
        </ol>
        <p>A wrong code shows the message “The code is incorrect or has already been used. Enter the next code from the app.” Wrong codes count towards the failed attempts limit (5 attempts — blocked for 15 minutes).</p>
    </HelpTopicSection>

    <HelpTopicSection Id="profile-sessions">
        <p>The <span class="help-ui">Other devices</span> card on the <span class="help-ui">Security</span> tab ends all your sign-ins except this browser. You will need it if you left yourself signed in on someone else's computer or lost your phone.</p>
        <ol class="help-steps">
            <li>Open <span class="help-ui">Profile</span> → the <span class="help-ui">Security</span> tab.</li>
            <li>In the <span class="help-ui">Other devices</span> card, click <span class="help-ui">Sign out on other devices</span> and confirm “Sign out on all other devices?”.</li>
            <li>The message “Signed out on other devices” appears.</li>
        </ol>
        <p>You stay signed in in this browser. Other devices lose access <strong>within a few minutes</strong> — as soon as their access token expires (at most 5 minutes); editing pages open there lose it in about a minute. After that, a new sign-in is needed on those devices.</p>
        <p>If you suspect someone else knows your password, change it (see “<a href="/help#account-change-password">Changing your password</a>”) — this also ends the sign-ins on all other devices.</p>
    </HelpTopicSection>
</HelpChapterSection>
